---
title: Copycat McDonald's Holiday Pie Recipe
description: This copycat McDonald's Holiday Pie brings back the nostalgic magic of the seasonal favorite with a flaky crust and creamy vanilla custard filling. Store-bought pie dough keeps things easy, while the rich, custardy center bakes up smooth, sweet, and comforting. Finished with a simple vanilla glaze, festive sprinkles, and a pinch of sea salt, these mini pies are warm, bakery-style treats that feel just as special at home as they do from the drive-thru.
servings: 8
cook time: 45 minutes
time required: 50 minutes
prep time: 5 minutes
source: https://tasty.co/recipe/copycat-mcdonalds-holiday-pie
cuisine: North American
author: Bay Nigro
nutrition:
course: Desserts
---

Preheat the oven to 400°F. Line a #baking sheet{} with parchment paper, and set aside.

Whisk together @vanilla pudding mix{1/2%(1.7-ounce) package}, @milk{1/2%cup}, @vanilla cake mix{2%tbsp},
and @vanilla extract{1%tsp} in a medium bowl until smooth.

In a separate mixing bowl, beat @cream cheese{5%oz}(softened) with a hand mixer fitted with the
beater attachment on medium speed until soft and fluffy, about ~{2%minutes}.
Fold in the pudding mixture until fully combined. Set aside.

Unroll the @pie crusts{2}(refrigerated) on a clean work surface, and trim away the rounded edges.
Cut each crust sheet into 8 squares (roughly 3.5").

Spoon about @filling{3%tbsp} of the filling onto 1 dough square, leaving a 1/2" border around the edges.
Lay a second dough square over the top, then gently press around the filling to smooth everything out and release any air.
Seal the edges using a fork. Place on the prepared baking sheet.
Repeat the filling and sealing process with the remaining dough squares and filling (you'll have 8 pies total).

Bake the pies until puffed and slightly golden, about ~{10-12%minutes}.

Whisk together @powdered sugar{1/2%cup}, @milk{1%tbsp}, and @sea salt{pinch} in a small bowl,
starting with 1 tablespoon of milk and adding up to 1 additional tablespoon as desired.
Drizzle the mixture over the warm pies, then finish with @festive sprinkle{}(for garnish)
while the glaze is still wet. Let the pies stand until the glaze is set, about ~{30%minutes}. 
Serve.

